@startuml federation_flow_with_localization
title Federation reference flow - Variant A (with a localization service)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 10
autonumber

actor "Consumer\n(Application tier)" as C
participant "openEHR Federation\n(gateway)" as F
participant "Localization service\n(proposed: IHE XCPD)" as L
participant "Addressing / directory\n(proposed: IHE mCSD)" as A
participant "PIX Manager\n(per community)" as P
participant "CDR + Query API\n(per node)" as D

C -> F : AQL, patient by ehr_status/subject = 123 (e.g. BSN)
note over F : Phase 0 - façade accepts openEHR AQL

F -> L : Localization (e.g. XCPD ITI-55)
L --> F : source communities where the patient\nexists AND has consent
F -> A : Addressing (e.g. mCSD) - resolve PIX Managers + CDR base URLs
A --> F : per-community PIX Manager + CDR URL

loop per candidate community
  F -> P : PIXm $ihe-pix (ITI-83)\nsourceIdentifier=123, targetSystem=ehrId
  P --> F : local ehr_id (or not-found)
end
note over F : Phase 1 done - set of {node, ehr_id, consent}

group per node with a resolved ehr_id AND consent granted
  F -> D : standard AQL  WHERE e/ehr_id/value = <local ehr_id>
  D --> F : rows (no subject involved)
end
note over F : Phase 3 - combine, DISTINCT / ORDER BY,\nre-inject subject if SELECTed, endpoint provenance, meta.endpoints[]
F --> C : combined result set {q, columns, rows} + meta
@enduml
